fixture cam_shaft_climb
doc BUILD.md s5 tech 5 "Wall-kick climb"; docs/adr/0011: a wall-cling is a rest height, so a climb moves the camera up in steady steps. The presses come every 24 ticks, the kick climb's period (ADR-0010), so every one finds the wall
room test/camera
spawn 4440 3200
frames 420
input
  # Holding toward the wall throughout; jump from the floor, then a kick at each apex.
  0..22 R jump
  23 R
  24..46 R jump
  47 R
  48..70 R jump
  71 R
  72..94 R jump
  95 R
  96..118 R jump
  119 R
  120..142 R jump
  143 R
  144..166 R jump
  167 R
  168..190 R jump
  191 R
  192..214 R jump
  215 R
  216..238 R jump
  239 R
  240..262 R jump
  263 R
  264..286 R jump
  287 R
  288..310 R jump
  311 R
  312..419 R
end
expect
  at 0 event.jump=1
  at 24 event.wall_kick=1
  never 0..419 event.air_jump=1
  mark top 100..419 event.land=1
  at top y=960u state=ground
end
